---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/print-on-demand';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for/print-on-demand');
const desc = description(site, 'for/print-on-demand');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Should a POD launch use sold-out messaging?",
    "answer": "Only when a real capacity, licensing or availability limit applies. Made-to-order availability alone does not justify an invented inventory shortage."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if personalized previews are unavailable?",
    "answer": "Use a secure draft or account link and explain the next step. Do not substitute a blank image or expose a private upload in a broadcast."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should production updates send?",
    "answer": "Use confirmed production events and an operational owner. Do not interpret payment or order creation as proof that the supplier has started printing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which tool should a POD store choose?",
    "answer": "Require a demonstration using your customizer, production events and purchase exclusions. Compare operating cost and contribution requirements without assuming an order-volume cutoff."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/for">All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Print-on-demand email: protect custom orders and production promises</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose email workflows around design interest, personalization state and supplier production events. A made-to-order catalog does not have the same inventory story as a warehouse of finished goods.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Distinguish a design launch from an inventory sale</h2>
    <p>Build an interest list for the design or niche and explain the creator story. Confirm that artwork rights, supplier availability and production capacity are cleared before announcing the launch. Use a real order cutoff or licensed release window when one exists; do not invent scarce stock for an indefinitely printable design.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Recover personalization without exposing customer artwork</h2>
    <p>Define separate events for customizer started, draft saved, approval needed, order placed and production locked. A draft reminder needs a working access-controlled link and an expiry policy. If the integration cannot supply a safe preview, link to the account or support route rather than emailing a blank mockup or an uploaded private photo. Stop reminders after purchase or draft deletion.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Give approval and production their own owners</h2>
    <p>Document which products require approval, who approves, when production begins and what changes remain possible. Order acknowledgement is not proof that a print partner accepted the job. Send delays from actual production status, with a support route and revised expectation approved by operations. Suppress cross-sell while artwork, quality or delivery issues remain unresolved.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Calculate offer room per design</h2>
    <p>Use net selling receipts less print base cost, shipping subsidy, payment costs, expected replacements and other relevant variable costs to set the offer budget. These inputs differ by print location, size and destination. A high revenue campaign can still lose contribution. Recalculate after supplier or shipping changes and check bundle discounts against every included variant.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Capture social interest with a useful promise</h2>
    <p>Let a visitor choose the design theme they want to hear about. Match the welcome message to that promise and show sizing, material and production information for the actual item. After a traffic spike, distinguish new niche subscribers from existing buyers. Do not assume all visitors want weekly releases or another channel simply because they arrived from social media.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Demonstration brief and proposed launch rehearsal</h2>
    <p>Ask Sequenzy and other shortlisted vendors to demonstrate interest capture through draft recovery, approval and purchase exclusion with your customizer and supplier events. This is a proposed test, not a capability claim. Rehearse a deleted draft, duplicate event, changed shipping estimate and refund before a real launch. Choose the simplest stack that preserves those handoffs and has a named operator.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Judge margin and handoff quality</h2>
    <p>Report personalization completion, approval wait, late production notices, replacements and contribution after discounts. Separate design interest from purchase attribution. A proposed launch-content experiment should compare eligible audiences with the same production window and include refunds and replacements before judging the result.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Service ownership and evidence</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications">Shopify store notifications</a> documents event-based order, fulfillment, refund, exchange and account notices. Assign each service event a sender before adding marketing automation; this source does not verify any third-party integration. Reviewed 24 November 2026.</p>
    <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment workflow</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch workflow</a></p>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
